# Capacity set of the adapters and examples (Capacity.h) for one ESP-IDF application. Each
# application's Kconfig.projbuild sources this file with rsource, and its component that compiles the
# adapter and example sources applies the values with motorcontrolcan_capacity_definitions
# (capacity.cmake). Zero selects the value Capacity.h derives from the channel count.
menu "MotorControl-CAN adapter capacity"
config MOTORCONTROLCAN_SDO_CHANNELS
    int "SDO channels (drive axis routes) on the CAN interface"
    default 2
    range 1 125
    help
        One channel per axis route. Sizes the SDO store, the owner's reservations and urgent
        slots, the TWAI TX slots and the application's sessions. A storage count only: the TWAI
        adapter submits one frame per service turn, so stopping N axes needs at least N turns,
        and owner CPU per turn and bus time limit how many axes are served at a given rate.
config MOTORCONTROLCAN_OWNER_REQUESTS
    int "Ordinary owner request slots (0: channels + 4, at least 6)"
    default 0
    range 0 250
    help
        Shared queued, active and unread ordinary requests. Channels plus requests must not
        exceed 255; Capacity.h refuses other values at compile time.
config MOTORCONTROLCAN_OWNER_PRODUCERS
    int "Owner fairness producers (0: channels + 2, at least 4)"
    default 0
    range 0 255
config MOTORCONTROLCAN_PDO_ROUTES
    int "Bound PDO wire routes on the CAN interface"
    default 8
    range 1 255
config MOTORCONTROLCAN_DISCOVERY_TARGETS
    int "Targets of one discovery plan (0: channels, at most 2)"
    default 0
    range 0 28
    help
        Larger scans run as several plans. At most the channel count.
endmenu
